Will Stuyvesant wrote:
>
> I am on level 6 with a monk, and found some interesting
> but unidentified stuff like a pink spellbook.  In an
> earlier game I did read an unidentifiedd spellbook and
> that killed me, so I don't do that again.  I have not
> found an altar yet, let alone an altar of my deity.

There is a guaranteed altar in the mines.  By level 6 you
will have found a level with two stairs leading down.  One
is to the rest of the main dungeon that is shaped much like
the levels you've been on before.  The other doesn't have
rooms and corridors in the same style.  You'll have quite
an adventure surviving down that path but the guaranteed
altar is that way as well as an item at least as valuable
as the altar even farther down.  With an altar you'll know
what is cursed and what is not.  Blessed spellbooks can
always be read, uncursed ones it depends on their level so
you just read a safe place, and the cursed ones are the
problems.

> I have found a potion shop and a general store.
>
> I found a lot of potions, but unidentified.  I also have
> some scrolls, also unidentified.  I have about 1000 gold
> (sold things).

You can narrow down the possibilities for each type of
item by seeing what the shopkeepier in the general shop
will offer you.  Drop, get an offer, decline, pick back up.
You can look up the prices in a spoiler or build a table
for yourself.

> And since everything I find is unidentified I dare not
> wield weapons or wear armor, I tried that before and then
> something was cursed and made the game awful.

There are ways to tell if something is cursed.  Hand a
weapon to an orc and if the ord wields it you'll know
whether it's cursed for example.  And you'll get to have
fun killing a heavily armed orc, so do it in a corridor
so you only face one at a time.

> What do you do?  Keep looking for holy water?  How to get
> holy water?  Go to the next level again and again?

In particular to into the mines.  If you get into trouble,
head back up into the shallower levels for a while to recover
then head down into the mines again.  I will typically clear
out one level parallel to the mines, and clear out one level
of the mines going back and forth until I've done both.
Lather rinse repeat until I've found the guaranteed altar.

> I also have the idea I should do something useful with all
> those fountains I see everywhere, but the things I tried
> killed me before.

Fountains have 30 possible outcomes.  Some that are dangerous
for low level characters aren't a challenge for high level
characters.  So patience.  Use them later.

